[29.55,"o","\r\n  GENE TRANSFER AND TISSUE CULTURE TECHNOLOGIES FOR IMPROVEMENT OF"]
[29.792,"o","\r\n  PEACH, SOYBEAN, AND TOBACCO"]
[29.792,"o","\r\n"]
[30.258,"o","\r\n                                                 GENERAL"]
[30.75,"o","\r\n              PRIMARY CLASSIFICATION         CLASSIFICATION"]
[30.75,"o","\r\n"]
[31.225,"o","\r\n        RPA   ACTVTY  CMMDTY  SCNCE   PRCNT    PRGM   JTC"]
[31.7,"o","\r\n        R304  A4900   C1000   F0513   042%     P3.13  J2A"]
[32.175,"o","\r\n        R304  A5000   C1000   F0312   028%     P3.13  J2A"]
[32.65,"o","\r\n        R307  A4900   C2300   F0312   015%     P3.06  J2A"]
[33.125,"o","\r\n        R307  A4900   C2600   F0312   015%     P3.11  J2A"]
[33.125,"o","\r\n"]
[33.658,"o","\r\n PRIMARY HEADINGS: R304 Biological Efficiency-Fruit, Vegetables;"]
[34.192,"o","\r\n R307 Biological Efficiency-Field Crops; A4900 Biology of Plants"]
[34.7,"o","\r\n and Animals; A5000 Biological Efficiency of Plants, Animals;"]
[35.242,"o","\r\n C1000 Deciduous and Small Fruits and Nuts; C2300 Soybeans; C2600"]
[35.75,"o","\r\n Tobacco; F0513 Genetics-Other; F0312 Biology-Molecular-Plant"]
[35.75,"o","\r\n"]
[36.3,"o","\r\n GENERAL HEADINGS: P3.13 Fruit; P3.06 Soybeans; P3.11 Tobacco; J2A"]
[36.442,"o","\r\n Plant Production"]
[36.442,"o","\r\n"]
[36.908,"o","\r\n                     SPECIAL CLASSIFICATION AND HEADINGS"]
[37.433,"o","\r\n         S1015   Peaches                                   070%"]
[37.958,"o","\r\n         S2610   Flue-Cured Tobacco                        015%"]
[37.958,"o","\r\n"]
[38.408,"o","\r\n      BASIC 080%    APPLIED 020%    DEVELOPMENTAL 000%"]
[38.408,"o","\r\n"]
[38.967,"o","\r\n  OBJECTIVES:   To   develop   tissue  culture  and  gene  transfer"]
[39.517,"o","\r\n techniques  to  improve  disease  resistance and morphogenesis in"]
[40.067,"o","\r\n peach,  soybean,  and tobacco and to determine the role of ABA in"]
[40.45,"o","\r\n root morphogenesis of tissue-cultured plants."]
[40.45,"o","\r\n"]
[41.008,"o","\r\n  APPROACH: 1) Investigations with peach, soybean, and tobacco will"]
[41.558,"o","\r\n focus  on  transfer-  ring  genes via Agrobacterium-mediated gene"]
[42.108,"o","\r\n transfer and electroporation. DNA to be transferred will carry an"]
[42.658,"o","\r\n antibiotic  resistance  marker to permit selection of transformed"]
[43.208,"o","\r\n cells  prior to regeneration and either phytohor- mone-specifying"]
[43.758,"o","\r\n genes  calculated  to  overcome our inability to regenerate peach"]
[44.308,"o","\r\n and  soybean  plants from cell cultures that confer resistance to"]
[44.858,"o","\r\n several  bacterial  pathogens.  2) Investigations with peach will"]
[45.408,"o","\r\n also  include  testing the response of peach regenerants in vitro"]
[45.958,"o","\r\n and  under  greenhouse  conditions  to several peach pathogens as"]
[46.508,"o","\r\n well  as evaluating the field performance of peach plants derived"]
[47.058,"o","\r\n from  tissue  cultures.  Immunofluorescence,  GC/MS  and electron"]
[47.608,"o","\r\n microscopy  techniques  will  be used to study the role of ABA in"]
[48.158,"o","\r\n root  formation  of in vitro propagated peach shoots. Beltsville,"]
[48.708,"o","\r\n MD;  BG  006,  Room  1,  BL-1; RD-35; 06/10/91. Scientists: F. A."]
[48.958,"o","\r\n Hammerschlag and L. D. Owens."]
[48.958,"o","\r\n"]
[49.517,"o","\r\n  KEYWORDS:  GENE-TRANSFER  TISSUE-CULTURE PEACHES SOYBEANS TOBACCO"]
[50.067,"o","\r\n PLANT-IMPROVEMENT TREE-IMPROVEMENT CROP-PRODUCTION PLANT-GENETICS"]
[50.617,"o","\r\n GENETIC-ENGINEERING  PLANT-DISEASE-RESISTANCE MORPHOGENESIS ROOTS"]
[51.125,"o","\r\n ROOT-DEVELOPMENT AGROBACTERIUM ANTIBIOTIC-RESISTANCE MARKERS"]
[51.125,"o","\r\n"]
[51.325,"o","\r\n  PROGRESS: 8708 TO 9207"]
[51.875,"o","\r\n Field studies of tissue-cultured (TC), own-rooted peach cultivars"]
[52.425,"o","\r\n indicated thatTC trees produced significantly more fruit compared"]
[52.975,"o","\r\n with bud-grafted trees 2 and 3 years after planting in the field."]
[53.525,"o","\r\n These  studies  should  be  of  interest  to scientists and peach"]
[54.075,"o","\r\n growers   since   they   demonstrate  the  feasibility  of  using"]
[54.625,"o","\r\n TC-propagation  to  produce  own-rooted  peach  trees. Through in"]
[55.175,"o","\r\n vitro  selection  and  screening  for  somaclonal variants, peach"]
[55.725,"o","\r\n plants  have  been  obtained  with  stable  increased  levels  of"]
[56.275,"o","\r\n resistance  to  Xanthomonas  campestris pv. pruni and Pseudomonas"]
[56.825,"o","\r\n syringae  pv.  syringae.  These  studies should be of interest to"]
[57.375,"o","\r\n other  scientists concerned with improving woody crop species. An"]
[57.925,"o","\r\n in  vitro  screening  system  for  evaluating peach germplasm for"]
[58.475,"o","\r\n root-knot  nematode  resistance  was  developed that shortens the"]
[59.025,"o","\r\n screening period from 3 years to 5 weeks. This system can be used"]
[59.575,"o","\r\n to  evaluate  seedlings  and  peach  plants  derived  from tissue"]
[60.125,"o","\r\n culture      and      genetic     engineering     studies.     An"]
[60.675,"o","\r\n Agrobacterium-mediated  gene  transfer  system for peach has been"]
[61.225,"o","\r\n developed  for  peach  which  has  been  used  to  introduce  the"]
[61.775,"o","\r\n cytokinin  gene  into  peach  and  will  be used as the basis for"]
[62.325,"o","\r\n future   gene   transfer   studies.  A  gene  vector  pGT100  was"]
[62.875,"o","\r\n constructed   for   use   with  the  supervirulent  Agrobacterium"]
[63.425,"o","\r\n tumefaciens  helper  strain  EHA101.  pGT100/EHA101 proved highly"]
[63.975,"o","\r\n efficient  in  transferring  genes  to tobacco and soybean. These"]
[64.525,"o","\r\n studies  may  lead to improved methods for scientists to transfer"]
[64.9,"o","\r\n genes to these difficult to transform crops."]
[64.9,"o","\r\n"]
